<section class="mr-section"><h2>Source and model boundaries</h2><p>${a(E)}</p><p>J. L. Heiberg, <cite>Euclidis opera omnia</cite>, vol.III, Leipzig: B. G. Teubner, 1886, pp.2–13. <a href="https://www.wilbourhall.org/pdfs/HeibergEuclidVolume_3.pdf">Complete source PDF</a>. Definition I.1 and the opening clause of I.2, selected clauses from X.2, and X.3’s statement appear in the reading. Full scans include X.1 and the continuing proof of X.3. Handwriting in the scanned copy is not part of the typeset text.</p><p>Line wrapping and end-of-line hyphenation are removed; geometric labels use Greek Unicode. Heiberg’s Latin u/v spelling and the Greek editorial brackets remain. Apparatus and inline reference markers omitted in selections remain in the whole-page images. English translations and grammar notes have not had independent philological peer review.</p><p>All subtraction counts, signs and zero decisions use exact BigInt arithmetic on (a + b√2)/d. Decimal values and SVG positions are rounded. The export records completed earlier turns and the actual partial current turn, without inventing further performed operations. The comparison table and recurrence proof are separate calculations. No physical instrument tolerance or ancient measurement accuracy is modeled.</p><p>This HTML embeds its twelve pages and local font; it has no scripts or network subresources. External links need a connection. Print formatting and PDF inspection do not establish a physical print’s dimensions or accessibility tagging.</p></section>
